                <pb facs="0184" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-30T21:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1928—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 31—10:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. Your telegram number 95, October 27, 5 p.m. In view of the reported presence
                    of Ferrera in western Honduras, President Paz requests as a precautionary
                    measure that the <hi rendition="#italic">Cleveland</hi> be permitted to remain
                    in Honduran waters for the present. However in my opinion there is now no
                    adequate reason why the ship should not depart at the end of this week.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Puerto Cortez.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
